statement:
You are given `arr`, a list of positive integers. Look at every binary tree that meets these rules:

- each node has either no children (a leaf) or exactly two children;
- reading the leaves from left to right (in-order) gives exactly the values of `arr`, in the same order;
- every non-leaf node holds the product of two numbers: the biggest leaf value in its left subtree and the biggest leaf value in its right subtree.

Over all such trees, return the minimum possible sum of the values held by the non-leaf nodes. That minimum is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit signed integer.

validator:
function validate([arr]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(arr) || arr.length < 2 || arr.length > 40) return 'arr needs 2 to 40 values.';
  if (arr.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 1 || v > 15)) return 'Each value is a whole number from 1 to 15.';
  return null;
}

